==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|cutis||living skin}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|cutes}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} The true [[skin]] or [[dermis]], underlying the [[epidermis]].
#* '''1883''': Alfred Swaine Taylor, Thomas Stevenson, ''The principles and practice of medical jurisprudence''
#*: The '''cutis''' measures in thickness from a quarter of a line to a line and a half (a line is one-twelfth of an inch).

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|corium}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|cutaneous}}
* {{l|en|cutin}}

===Anagrams===
* {{l|en|ictus}}

