==Latin==

===Etymology===
From {{der|la|ine-pro|*kuH-t-}}, [[zero-grade]] without [[s-mobile]] form of {{m|ine-pro|*(s)kewH-||to cover}}. Cognates include Welsh {{m|cy|cwd||scrotum}}, Lithuanian {{m|lt|kutỹs||purse}} and Old English {{m|ang|hȳd}} (English {{m|en|hide}}). Related to {{m|la|obscūrus||dark, obscure}} and {{m|la|culus||ass}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{la-IPA|cutis}}

===Noun===
{{la-noun|cutis||cutis|f|third}}

# {{lb|la|anatomy}} [[living]] [[skin]]
# [[rind]], [[surface]]
# [[hide]], [[leather]]

====Inflection====
{{la-decl-3rd-I|cutis}}

